WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV — satiation (60s) AI-synthesized studio narration

1
00:00:01.604 --> 00:00:05.422
Bulls assume every prompt wants unbounded compute forever;

2
00:00:05.422 --> 00:00:08.648
skeptics assume finite tasks cap total AI demand.

3
00:00:12.791 --> 00:00:15.684
Splitting total demand into number of tasks times

4
00:00:15.684 --> 00:00:18.932
compute per task resolves both errors in one framework.

5
00:00:23.076 --> 00:00:27.104
Individual tasks hit a sharp utility plateau at verification,

6
00:00:27.104 --> 00:00:31.067
while falling unit cost unlocks previously uneconomic tasks.

7
00:00:35.211 --> 00:00:43.129
Competition compresses software markups, pushing long-run marginal cost down toward physical electricity and hardware amortization.

8
00:00:47.272 --> 00:00:52.941
Because finished tasks satiate, winning architectures hit the finish line at minimum joules per task.
